<h1>about</h1>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>who's running this</h2>
  <p class="prompt">sp3ctr. one person, one text editor, no team, no
    investors, no roadmap but my own.</p>
  <p>i built this node because the mainstream web stopped feeling like
    mine a long time ago — every page a funnel, every word a training
    set, every click logged for someone else's benefit. this is the
    opposite of that: static files, no analytics, no accounts, nothing
    collected. what you see in your browser is the whole system.</p>
  <p>governments call it national security. corporations call it
    personalization. underneath, it's the same basic move: watch
    everyone, so you can act on anyone. capability like that doesn't stay
    pointed where it started — it gets turned on journalists, organizers,
    and whistleblowers the moment they're inconvenient enough to matter.</p>
  <p>i care about privacy as something we owe each other, not just
    something to configure for yourself. i care about tools staying in
    the hands of the people who need them, not locked behind platforms
    that can be bought, sold, or subpoenaed. this site is a small,
    low-stakes way of practicing that.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>a few honest rules</h2>
  <p>trust but verify — that includes me. don't take a claim on faith
    because it's confidently stated; check the source, read the code, do
    the math yourself.</p>
  <p>stay safe out there. encrypt what actually matters, keep backups of
    what you can't afford to lose, and look out for the people around
    you. they can't stop us all — but only if we act like it.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>reach the node</h2>
  <p>no contact form, no tracking pixel behind one. if you know where to
    find me, you already know how. if you don't yet — check back, that
    may change.</p>
</section>
